Add :class:`icalendar.StreamingCalendarParser`, a feed/finish-style parser for large calendars that arrive in chunks. Each top-level calendar subcomponent is delivered as soon as it is complete, independently of how the input is split into chunks. Components referring to timezones defined later in the stream are buffered (with a configurable limit) instead of being delivered with a guessed timezone. Resource limits for line length, nesting depth, component size, and the pending-timezone buffer can be configured with :class:`icalendar.StreamLimits`. Create one with :meth:`icalendar.Calendar.streaming_parser`.
